                        <forename>Richard Lalor</forename>
                        <surname>Shiel</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1791-08-17">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1851-05-23"/>
                    <occupation>playwright</occupation>
                    <occupation>politician</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Shiel was a noted dramatist and later a politician who was one of the founding members of the Catholic Association, the organization 
    set up by Danial O'Connell in 1823 to campaign for Catholic Emancipation.  His plays were performed in Dublin and London. He was later elected MP for Milborne 
    Port  in 1830 and Louth in 1831.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">W. Torrens McCullagh, <title>Memoirs of Richard Lalor Sheil</title> (Hurst &amp; Blackett, 1855), 2 vols.</bibl>
